.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Rasterized glyph cache\&. 

Internal header\&.
.PP
Rasterizing a glyph is expensive and the same glyphs recur constantly, so every rasterized glyph is kept, keyed by its font and glyph index\&. A cache entry holds the rasterized pixels plus the offsets needed to place them against the pen position\&.
.PP
Entries are individually allocated rather than packed into one large atlas texture\&. Packing exists to let a GPU draw many glyphs with one texture binding, and Schultz rasterizes on the CPU, so it would buy locality but not batching, so it is not worth what it costs until something draws on a GPU\&.
.PP
\fBNot part of the host facing interface\&.\fP Rasterized glyphs, kept for the renderer\&. A host binds to \fBschultz_api\&.h\fP; this header is the toolkit's own and may change without notice\&. 
.PP
Definition in file \fBschultz_glyphs\&.h\fP\&.
