.SH "Enumeration Type Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "anonymous enum"

.PP
What the bytes of a rasterized glyph mean\&. A letter is a shape with no colour of its own, so it rasterizes to coverage: how much of each pixel the shape covered\&. The colour arrives later, from the style, and the painter multiplies the two\&. That is what lets one face draw text in any colour\&.
.PP
An emoji is a picture and brings its own colours, so there is nothing for the style to say\&. It rasterizes to finished pixels and the painter copies them, using the style's colour only for how solid the whole thing is\&. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_GLYPH_COVERAGE \fP\fP
One byte per pixel: how much of the pixel the shape covered\&. 
.TP
\fB\fISCHULTZ_GLYPH_COLOR \fP\fP
Four bytes per pixel, blue green red alpha, already multiplied\&. 
.PP
